+
+## D034: Bounded diagnosis deadline and explicit uncertainty, November 2, 2026
+
+A local photo trial returned a generic failure after 20.25 seconds. Its private
+wrapper discarded the original error, so timing is consistent with a timeout
+but does not prove the provider-side cause. The old unknown outcome and usage
+remain unresolved in the original journal.
+
+Diagnosis now uses the existing 30-second transport maximum and zero automatic
+retries. Other gateway defaults remain unchanged. Timeout and uncertain-outcome
+messages explain that provider processing/usage may remain unknown and direct
+operators to inspect status before a new request. Raw provider errors remain
+redacted; the browser uses its own safe messages.
+
+The user's explicit request to retry after repair and demonstrate a final manual
+also permits a separate, visibly SYNTHETIC local project using existing fixture
+measurements. That isolated adapter scopes synthetic compilation to one owner,
+project, inventory revision, data directory and trusted context. Production
+synthetic acceptance remains disabled. Actual live proposals still pass through
+the compiler and renderer, and fixture SVGs remain watermarked. No physical work
+or test pass may be fabricated. Each new live run retains finite, nonrenewing
+controls, durable reservations and a halt on unknown outcomes; the old journal
+is neither reset nor represented as settled.
+
+The connected retest exposed an unusable diagnosis with known usage of 2,048
+output tokens. This suggests the previous completion cap was reached, but the
+original finish reason was not retained, so truncation is not proven. Diagnosis
+now requests at most three short entries per category and a bounded 4,096-token
+completion allowance; other proposals retain 2,048. Incomplete output remains
+rejected, with no automatic retry. The same finite window permitted one reviewed
+diagnosis repair/retest by removing unused design allocation, without renewal.
+
+Live acceptance then succeeded: photo intake, a real two-call Muse design
+proposal accepted by the compiler, eight rendered manual panels, explicit plan
+activation, and diagnosis with active fold-step context. The final diagnosis
+finished normally in 21,703 ms (4,879 input / 1,827 output tokens). The five calls
+in this session used 15,505 input / 7,308 output tokens, including the unusable
+diagnosis; these are provider usage, not a monetary price or free-call claim.
+There are zero physical progress events. The manual and measurements are
+synthetic, physical verification remains not_attempted, and production defaults
+still reject synthetic evidence. Local exported artifacts are in the workspace's
+output directory; the private journals preserve the original unknown usage.
